{"id":"8306a79d3c8e988a","group":"58","path":"58/batch20/58-df-shift.md","title":"Shift","display":"df-shift — Shift","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-shift","aliases":["58-df-shift","Shift"],"display":"df-shift — Shift","depends_on":["[[58-df-symbolic-dynamics]]","[[58-df-function]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-shift"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-shift</span><span>Shift</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-shift — Shift"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"a2e7cac8985289f7\" href=\"?note=a2e7cac8985289f7\" title=\"58-df-symbolic-dynamics\">58-df-symbolic-dynamics</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"58-df-function\">58-df-function</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A,\\sigma_A\\in V\">\\(A,\\sigma_A\\in V\\)</span> with <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A\\neq\\varnothing\">\\(A\\neq\\varnothing\\)</span> (alphabet and shift graph)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"F_A\\in V\">\\(F_A\\in V\\)</span> is the set of bi-infinite <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A\">\\(A\\)</span>-valued function graphs</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ShiftMap}_S(\\sigma_A;A,F_A)\">\\(\\mathrm{ShiftMap}_S(\\sigma_A;A,F_A)\\)</span> (shift-map relation defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}shift}\\vdash \\mathrm{ShiftMap}_S(\\sigma_A;A,F_A)\\leftrightarrow A\\neq\\varnothing\\land F_A=\\{x\\in\\mathcal P(\\mathbb Z\\times A):\\mathrm{Function}(x,\\mathbb Z,A)\\}\\land\\mathrm{Function}(\\sigma_A,F_A,F_A)\\land\\forall x\\in F_A\\;\\forall i\\in\\mathbb Z\\;\\bigl(\\sigma_A(x)(i)=x(i+1)\\bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}shift}\\vdash \\mathrm{ShiftMap}_S(\\sigma_A;A,F_A)\\leftrightarrow A\\neq\\varnothing\\land F_A=\\{x\\in\\mathcal P(\\mathbb Z\\times A):\\mathrm{Function}(x,\\mathbb Z,A)\\}\\land\\mathrm{Function}(\\sigma_A,F_A,F_A)\\land\\forall x\\in F_A\\;\\forall i\\in\\mathbb Z\\;\\bigl(\\sigma_A(x)(i)=x(i+1)\\bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Shift: shifts sequence index by 1; fundamental in symbolic dynamics</li>\n<li>Both the sequence carrier <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"F_A\">\\(F_A\\)</span> and the shift graph are explicit set objects.</li>\n<li>Shift space: closed <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\sigma\">\\(\\sigma\\)</span>-invariant subsets of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A^\\mathbb{Z}\">\\(A^\\mathbb{Z}\\)</span>; subshifts</li>\n<li>SFT: shift of finite type; defined by a finite list of forbidden blocks or by a finite graph</li>\n<li>A sofic shift is a sliding-block factor of a shift of finite type.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Lind and Marcus, An Introduction to Symbolic Dynamics</li>\n<li>Kitchens, Symbolic Dynamics</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-symbolic-dynamics","status":"resolved","id":"a2e7cac8985289f7","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-symbolic-dynamics]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-function","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-function]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"A,\\sigma_A\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"A\\neq\\varnothing","display":false},{"tex":"F_A\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"A","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{ShiftMap}_S(\\sigma_A;A,F_A)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}shift}\\vdash \\mathrm{ShiftMap}_S(\\sigma_A;A,F_A)\\leftrightarrow A\\neq\\varnothing\\land F_A=\\{x\\in\\mathcal P(\\mathbb Z\\times A):\\mathrm{Function}(x,\\mathbb Z,A)\\}\\land\\mathrm{Function}(\\sigma_A,F_A,F_A)\\land\\forall x\\in F_A\\;\\forall i\\in\\mathbb Z\\;\\bigl(\\sigma_A(x)(i)=x(i+1)\\bigr)","display":true},{"tex":"F_A","display":false},{"tex":"\\sigma","display":false},{"tex":"A^\\mathbb{Z}","display":false}],"bytes":1294,"backlinks":[{"id":"2751a859d290ac09","anchor":"ref-7","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$\\sigma_A$ is the two-sided shift graph defined in [[58-df-shift]]"},{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-1154","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch20/58-df-shift.md|58-df-shift]]（batch20）"}],"outgoing":["a2e7cac8985289f7","36d7463d215be751"]}